  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1134 AM MST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nThursday through Saturday... As the Wed/Thurs system leaves our area \non Thursday, a brief period of ridging will bring quiet, dry \nconditions on Thursday night and into Friday. A new system \napproaches the area Friday afternoon, with a positively tilted upper \nlevel trough in place over Colorado. This new system will be weaker \nthan the previous one, considering its unfavorable structure and \ntiming, leaving it with weak forcing and little moisture. \nPrecipitation is expected to be very meager with this system. Should \nnorthwest flow strengthen, there is the possibility for snow \naccumulation over the Central Mountains. We will continue to monitor \nthis system as it develops. By early Saturday, the system will be \nexiting our area. Expect breezy and dry weather through the weekend \nas the wave moves through. Near seasonal temps are forecast with \nhighs in the 50s and 60s and overnight lows in the 20s and 30s.\n\nSunday through Tuesday... After the weaker Fri/Sat system leaves our \narea, ridging develops and dominates through the rest of the period. \nQuiet, dry weather is expected across our CWA. Seasonal to above \nseasonal temps are forecast as we get into early next week. Highs \nwill be in the 50s and 60s, with some locations in the plains having \nthe potential to get up to 70. Lows in the 20s and 30s, up to 40 in \nthe eastern plains.",
